  "description": "Construction of a single storey rear extension with associated ramp access to the side",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of design and scale, would present an irregular form, would fail to appear subordinate to the host dwelling and would appear overbearing. It would therefore fail to reflect the character and appearance of the original dwelling and the character and design of the terrace row. The proposal is therefore contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that development recognises local character and promotes good design:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)Policies SP2, DMD1, and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
